course: dictionary
lesson: 2751
title: Words for disappointment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To disappoint someone means to make them sad because something was not as good as they hoped. It can also mean to let someone down by not doing what they expected.
explain: «The Rat gives in, because he can't bear to disappoint his friends.» The Rat does not want his friends to feel let down, so he gives in. The clue is «can't bear»: he really does not want to make them sad.
explain: «He hated disappointing people, and he was fond of the Mole.» Hated tells you he did not want to let people down. Fond of the Mole shows he cared about his friend, so he did not want to hurt him either.
explain: Look at the word forms. Disappointed describes how you feel, and disappointing describes what caused the feeling. Phrases to notice: disappointed in someone, disappointed with something, and I'm sorry to disappoint you.
fact: Disappoint is a verb. Its other forms are disappoints, disappointed and disappointing.
fact: «Disappoint» means to make someone sad because something was not as good as they hoped.
fact: «Disappoint» can also mean to let someone down by not doing what they expected.
fact: «Disappointed» describes how you feel; «disappointing» describes what made you feel that way.
fact: Common phrases: «disappointed in someone», «disappointed with something», «I'm sorry to disappoint you».
exercise: «The Rat gives in, because he can't bear to disappoint his friends.» What does disappoint mean here? | *To let his friends down | To give his friends a present | To go on a long journey | To make his friends laugh
exercise: Mia says, «The rain spoiled our picnic, it was so disappointing.» What does disappointing describe? | A person who is very tall | A kind of birdsong | A happy surprise | *Something that was not as good as she hoped
exercise: Which word describes how you feel when your hopes are not met? | disappoints | disappointing | disappoint | *disappointed
test: «He hated disappointing people, and he was fond of the Mole.» What does hated show about how he felt? | He forgot everyone's names | He was very tired | He liked making people sad | *He did not want to let people down
test: «I was disappointed with the film.» What does disappointed mean here? | Very hungry after the long film | Sleepy after lunch | Surprised by a loud noise | *Felt let down because it was not as good as I hoped
exam: «The team was ___ with the result, because they had hoped to win.» | disappointing | *disappointed | disappoint | disappoints
